// bisect: fusion/JIT bug (interp != jit) — FIXED, kept as regress pin
// Found by soak jul30a reactive lane (seed 2612000000 range, 2026-07-31,
// campaign binary 73de0cab); minimized by hand from divergence_000000.
// Pre-fix: interp Trace([0:i64:-1]; [0:i64:9]; [0:i64:-1])
//          jit    Trace([0:i64:-1]; [0:i64:9]; [0:i64:0])
// root_cause: interior op-cache memory across arm DESELECTION differed.
// `Cached::sleep` cleared the resident value, so on re-selection a
// bottoming interior op (1/v0 at v0=0) had no cache to ride, the arm
// body produced nothing, and the becoming-selected fire fell back to
// the arm wrapper's surviving cache (-1, the epoch-0 output). The
// kernel's honor-gated replay words persist across deselection, so it
// rode the div's stale word (1) and computed in0-1 = 0. Continuously-
// selected and first-selection variants agreed all along (combineLatest
// rides / no-history silence).
// RULING (Eric, 2026-07-31): 0 is right — sleep is PAUSE, value-channel
// caches survive it; the kernel semantics stand and `Cached::sleep`
// preserves the resident value. Both backends now emit 0 at epoch 2.
// schedule-v1: cap=144 events=1152; in1=bool:true; in1=bool:false in0=i64:1
{let v0 = i64:1 - in0; select in1 {true => i64:9, _ => in0 - (i64:1 / v0)}}
